## Context

"Easy to uninstall" is a corollary of *stateless* + *standalone*, and it is
the kindest property for someone trying erg out: they can back out cleanly.
It is also mechanically falsifiable — unlike a one-shot round-trip, test it
as a **matrix** of real routes with usage in between (you never uninstall a
pristine install; you uninstall after working).

**Finding up front:** there is *no* `erg uninstall` command, no uninstall
Makefile target, and no uninstall docs today — removal is entirely manual and
undocumented. This ticket tests the manual route and *documents* it; whether
to add an `erg uninstall` command is a separate feature decision (needs
evidence), not assumed here.

## The matrix (each cell round-trips to a byte-identical tree, zero orphans)

- **Install routes:** (a) `erg init` into a fresh `tickets/`; (b) the
  `install-erg-binary` Makefile path; (c) committed bootstrap binary + the
  pre-commit hook from `integration.md`.
- **Usage in between:** create / close / tag / log / rm / archive a few
  tickets and run `list`/`ready`/`check` — exercise the tool so the store and
  any side effects are non-trivial before removal.
- **Uninstall routes:** (a) documented manual removal (`rm tickets/erg`, the
  hook, generated assets); (b) `erg uninstall` *if/when* it exists.
- **Assertion:** after uninstall, everything *except the user's own ticket
  files* is byte-identical to pre-install (snapshot diff); no orphaned
  dotfiles, caches, or hooks. Whether the user's tickets are removed is an
  explicit, documented choice.

## Constraints

Shell, throwaway tempdir + `$HOME`, offline, deterministic; snapshot the tree
before install and after uninstall and diff.

## Relevant files

- `tests/test_roundtrip.sh` (new) + `Makefile` `TEST_SUITES += roundtrip`.
- `src/go/init.go`, the `install-erg-binary` target, `integration.md` (the
  documented manual-uninstall steps live or land here).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each install × uninstall route round-trips to a clean tree *after real
      usage*; orphan check passes.
- [ ] The manual-uninstall steps are documented (integration.md) and the test
      follows them exactly.
- [ ] What uninstall does/doesn't delete (the user's tickets) is explicit.
- [ ] Wired into `make test`; green.

## Notes

- The narrower "read commands write nothing outside the store" snapshot stays
  in 0146 (stateless). This ticket owns the install/uninstall *lifecycle*.
- Prior art (closed): 0029 (init/uninstall round-trip), 0032 (implement
  init/uninstall), 0082 (init simplified to unpack-only). Reconcile with
  whatever those left in place.
